Quadibloc wrote:
> On Jan 7, 9:17 pm, Charles Richmond <friz...@tx.rr.com> wrote:
> 
>> I *like* the "small capitals" font!!! I find it quaint and sort
>> of cute. Since I *learned* APL on this font (and a similar one
>> on a Tel-Ray terminal), my opinion is somewhat biased, admittedly.
> 
> And I learned APL on a 2741, which explains _my_ biases.
> 

Since I was used to the DECWriter font, I felt that the 2741
font looked a little "overdone". But I have to admit... the
2741 font *did* duplicate *much* better using the spirit
duplicators that professors used for examinations at the time.

Some professors resorted to handwritten APL tests if they did
*not* have access to a Selectric with a 2741 typeball. (There
did *not* seem to be any 2741 terminals on campus.) The APL
symbols in the DECWriter font were practically unreadable when
used with the spirit duplicators.


