Back around March 15-17 of 2008, I posted a question about how to set
up a KFQSA with external drives in a BA23 type enclosure.    This
weekend, I succeeded in getting DSSI drives going, so thought I'd post
my process here in appreciation for those who helped me.

My test system ended up being a Vaxstation III in a BA11: KA650 CPU,
MS650 16mb RAM, VCB01 video controller, KFQSA DSSI controller with an
RF30 DSSI ISE (drive).   The RF30 is connected directly to the KFQSA
and sits in the bottom of my H9642 cabinet along with a PC power
supply.   Theoretically, with the right cables, a standard SCSI-2
enclosure could be used for a neater installation, and I'll likely try
this later.

To get DSSI drive working directly with KA650/KFQSA:

Process requires a CPU monitor with advanced console commands like
CONFIGURE
 and SET HOST/DUP/UQSSP/DISK 0, thus cannot be done with firmware
  that's too old.. like is what on my KA630 CPU.

power cable:
- created power adapter harness to plug from standard 4 pin PC PSU
drive plug
    into the 5 pin molex DSSI power receptacle.  Pins 4+5 both go to
red +5V.

data cable:
- used Berg50 female -> Berg50 male cable as an extender from KFQSA.
- used Berg50 female -> Berg50 female -> miniD50 cable as the bus
cable.
- attached standard DEC DSSI terminator to miniD50.
- attached drive to open Berg50.

drive:
- set node ID switches / jumpers to zero (or whatever).

setup:
- set switches 1-4 of KFQSA to ON OFF ON ON to allow programming at
fixed
  CSR 0774420 (other options possible -- see KFQSA manual p. 4-4).

- at console, used CONFIGURE to select physical CSR for one ISE
(RF30).

  >>> configure
    device,number? kfqsa-disk,1
    device,number? exit

  system responded with recommendation:

  -772150/154 KFQSA-DISK
   >>>

programming:
- entered service mode

  >>> set host/uqssp/maintenance/service 0
     ('0' is for CSR address 774420 see page 6-3 for others)


  at configuration table prompt, I entered:

  ? clear 0                      (ie. remove any old def for node 0)
  ? set 0 772150 21              (ie. set NODE CSR TYPE (21 =3D disk))
  ? show                         (ie. just to check work entered)
  ? exit                         (ie. program it in)


test:
- shut down the power, and set switch 1 of KFQSA to OFF.  Others
untouched.
- repowered.
- did SHOW QBUS and SHOW UQSSP to verify presence of controller and
drive.

>>>show qbus
Scan of Qbus I/O Space
-20001468 (772150) =3D 0000 (154) RQDX3/KDA50/RRD50/RQC25/KFQSA-DISK
-2000146A (772152) =3D 0AB0
-20001F40 (777500) =3D 0020 (004) IPCR

Scan of Qbus Memory Space
>>>show uqssp
UQSSP Disk Controller 0 (772150)
-DUA0 (RF30)

- next, talked directly to drive ISE using ISE commands.

>>>set host/dup/uqssp/disk 0 direct       (ie. show directory of programs o=
n ISE)
Starting DUP server...

UQSSP Disk Controller 0 (772150)
Copyright =A9 1988  Digital Equipment Corporation
DRVEXR V1.0  D  5-JUL-1988 15:33:06
DRVTST V1.0  D  5-JUL-1988 15:33:06
HISTRY V1.0  D  5-JUL-1988 15:33:06
ERASE  V1.0  D  5-JUL-1988 15:33:06
PARAMS V1.0  D  5-JUL-1988 15:33:06
DIRECT V1.0  D  5-JUL-1988 15:33:06
End of directory

Stopping DUP server...
>>>set host/dup/uqssp/disk 0 histry       (ie. show history of drive)
Starting DUP server...

UQSSP Disk Controller 0 (772150)
Copyright =A9 1988  Digital Equipment Corporation
RF30
EN83704213
DIA0
1
RFX V101
RF30 PCB-5/ECO-00
48061                                   (ie. lifetime hours used)
192                                     (ie. lifetime power cycles)
Complete.

Stopping DUP server...
>>>set host/dup/uqssp/disk 0 erase
Starting DUP server...

UQSSP Disk Controller 0 (772150)
Copyright =A9 1988  Digital Equipment Corporation
Write/read anywhere on medium? [1=3DYes/(0=3DNo)] 1
User data will be corrupted.  Proceed? [1=3DYes/(0=3DNo)] 1
  6 minutes to complete.

....
end of doc.
....




