underscored raised smallcaps started with IBM, I believe

as shown in the earlier link to VT100 pages, the DECWriter had no 
descenders, so that, e.g, lowercase 'g' was raised so that its tail sat 
on the baseline  --  as you say, horrendously unattractive

I had an AJ version of the DECWriter, before acquiring a daisy printer 
--  I had to use it for business correspondence, since the only other 
options were to handwrite it, or tap it out on a rather klunky typewriter

when the lease expired, a year or two later, nobody bothered to collect 
the machine, which struck me as a reasonable assessment of its residual 
value

dear me, that daisy printer was a major step out of the primeval slime

